      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Marketing Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Marketing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Marketing Department 221510 - Marketing Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0089P Position Summary The Department of Marketing at La Salle University has an ongoing need for qualified adjunct faculty to teach a variety of courses each semester on an “as needed” basis. These undergraduate and/or graduate courses may include: Principles of Marketing, Marketing Management, Business-to-Business Marketing, Sports Marketing, and Digital Marketing. Courses may be offered in-person or online. Essential Duties • Teach assigned course(s). • Prepare and deliver course material consistent with departmental and school learning objectives, policies and guidelines. • Provide timely grading and feedback to students. • Provide guidance and support to students. Required Qualifications • Master’s degree in Business, Marketing or a related major. • Applicants with significant industry experience relating to the topic will be considered. • Knowledge and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Preferred Qualifications • Ph.D. in Business, Marketing or closely related major. • Previous teaching experience. • Flexibility in class scheduling. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours • Some classes offered may be in the evenings, on weekends, or online. Special Instructions to Applicant This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 10/27/2022 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Teaching Evaluations Transcript(s) Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
