    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/6394": {
      "title": "La Salle University Job Applicant Site",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Public Safety Captain Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Public Safety Captain Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. La Salle University offers its eligible employees comprehensive medical and dental plans, employer paid life and disability insurance, retirement benefits, generous paid time off (vacation, sick leave, and holidays), and tuition benefits such as no cost undergraduate and graduate degree programs for its employees (with no wait period) and no cost undergraduate degree programs for its employees’ dependents (after completing the required years of service). Position Details Position Overview Position Title Public Safety Captain Department 322000 – Public Safety Position Type Regular Position Classification Full-Time, 12 months Grant/Gift Funded (all or a portion)? No If Temporary or Grant Funded, Start Date and End Date Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number S1446P Position Summary The Public Safety Captain is responsible for coordinating the administrative and operational functions of an assigned patrol division. The Captain supervises Lieutenants and Sergeants, coordinates staffing plans, schedules, payroll review, training activities, and special event operations, while ensuring department policies and the operational priorities established by the Director of Public Safety are consistently implemented. Essential Duties Coordinates shift staffing, schedules, overtime assignments, and leave requests. Reviews payroll and attendance records prior to submission for final approval. Supervises Lieutenants and Sergeants and provides performance coaching. Reviews incident reports, patrol logs, and operational documentation. Coordinates staffing for University events and emergency operations. Conducts inspections of personnel, equipment, and assigned facilities. Ensures compliance with departmental directives and University policy. Responds to significant incidents requiring supervisory command. Maintains accountability for vehicles, radios, keys, uniforms, and departmental assets. Coordinates training and monitors required certifications. Secondary Responsibilities Assists with hiring processes. Prepares operational reports. Serves in the on-call rotation. Performs other assigned duties. # of Direct Reports 10 Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED required; associate degree or higher preferred. Minimum of three years of experience in campus public safety, security, law enforcement, military, or a closely related field. Demonstrated supervisory, leadership, communication, and report-writing skills. Valid driver’s license with the ability to meet University driving standards. Pennsylvania Act 235 certification or the ability to obtain Act 235 certification within six (6) months of appointment. Ability to exercise sound judgment and maintain professionalism during emergency situations. Knowledge of and commitment to the mission and values of the University. Preferred Qualifications Associate’s degree or higher. Previous experience in a higher education public safety environment. Working knowledge of Clery Act, Title IX, and VAWA requirements. Previous experience supervising personnel in a 24-hour operation. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours Ability to sit, stand, walk, climb stairs, and operate a vehicle for extended periods. Ability to lift up to 50 pounds. Ability to work weekends, holidays, and during University emergencies. Position is designated as essential personnel. Special Instructions to Applicant La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. La Salle University offers its eligible employees comprehensive medical and dental plans, employer paid life and disability insurance, retirement benefits, generous paid time off (vacation, sick leave, and holidays), and tuition benefits such as no cost undergraduate and graduate degree programs for its employees (with no wait period) and no cost undergraduate degree programs for its employees’ dependents (after completing the required years of service). Posting Information Application Open Date 07/30/2026 Application Close Date 12/31/2026 Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education you have completed (at the time of application)? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree Doctorate Degree (e.g., PhD, PsyD, JD) None of the above * Please select the answer that best describes your status in regards to the PA Act 235 and PA Act 120 certifications. I do not currently have nor will I be able to obtain either certification I do not currently have either certifications but am able to obtain one or both I currently have only my PA Act 235 certification I currently have only my PA Act 120 certification I currently have both my PA Act 235 and PA Act 120 certifications * What shifts are you available to work? 1130 PM to 8 AM Shift 730 AM to 4 PM Shift 330 PM to 12 AM Shift * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
