    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/5840": {
      "title": "La Salle University Job Applicant Site",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Public Safety Security Desk Receptionist (Part-Time, 12-Months) Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Public Safety Security Desk Receptionist (Part-Time, 12-Months) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All Public Safety Security Desk Receptionist positions are represented by the International Union, Security, Police and Fire Professionals of America (SPFPA) and are subject to the terms and conditions of a Collective Bargaining Agreement. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply. Position Details Position Overview Position Title Public Safety Security Desk Receptionist (Part-Time, 12-Months) Department 322000 - Public Safety Position Type Regular Position Classification Part-Time, 12 months Grant/Gift Funded (all or a portion)? No If Temporary or Grant Funded, Start Date and End Date N/A Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number S1038P Position Summary The primary purpose of the Security Desk Receptionist ( SDR ) is to verify the status of all persons desiring access through the buildings and facilities of La Salle University. The SDRs are charged with enforcing their duties: responsibly, proficiently and professionally. The SDR is responsible for the safety of University students, staff and faculty members, visitors, and the campus and property of the University. SDRs provide security at designated posts, enforce University policies, and document incidents occurring on campus and/or involving members of the La Salle Community. The Office of Public Safety is a 24 hour/day, 365 day/year operation. Public Safety Officers are considered essential personnel and are assigned to an eight-hour shift. Essential Duties Security, monitoring and controlling entry and exit in University facilities. Observing and controlling individuals and materials entering and leaving University facilities. Positioning oneself at or near the entrance of the University facilities. Observing individuals as they enter and leave the facilities. Confronting individuals who may not be permitted to enter University facilities, or who are attempting to leave University facilities with University property without proper authorization. File required reports as necessary. Maintain professional uniform and grooming standards. Knowledge of and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Secondary Responsibilities Works safely without presenting a direct threat to you or to others. Attend roll call, workshops and training sessions as required. May perform other tasks as directed or assigned by Supervisor or Security management. # of Direct Reports 0 Required Qualifications High School diploma or equivalent. Proficient in the use of MS Word, Excel, Power Point, Access, internet search software, and function specific databases. Must be able to communicate effectively by telephone, departmental radio system, or in a person-to-person setting. Excellent communication and customer service skills. Must be able to produce written documents with clearly organized thoughts. Preferred Qualifications 2 years of security experience Valid driver’s license Knowledge of safety and security issues within a higher education setting Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours Must be capable of standing or sitting for extended periods of time. Special Instructions to Applicant All Public Safety Security Desk Receptionist positions are represented by the International Union, Security, Police and Fire Professionals of America ( SPFPA ) and are subject to the terms and conditions of a Collective Bargaining Agreement. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply. Posting Information Application Open Date 06/04/2024 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education you have completed (at the time of application)? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree Doctorate Degree (e.g., PhD, PsyD, JD) None of the above * How many years of experience do you have in a related position? None Less than 3 years 3-5 years 6-8 years More than 8 years * Are you proficient in using a computer and software such as Microsoft Word and Excel? Yes No * Which shift(s) would you be available to work? 11pm-7am 7am-3pm 3pm-11pm * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
