    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/4895": {
      "title": "La Salle University Job Applicant Site",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Undergraduate Psychology, History and Systems of Psychology (in person) Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Undergraduate Psychology, History and Systems of Psychology (in person) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a course specific position announcement for an in-person section of PSY 430 \"History and Systems of Psychology\" at the undergraduate level for Spring 2024 . The course description is as follows: This course examines the beginnings and development of psychology as a science and profession; psychology's historical roots in philosophy, biology, and national culture. If you are interested in other teaching opportunities in Psychology, please see the general Psychology Undergraduate position announcement. There are other ads for specific pools for teaching in the Masters and Doctoral programs. Here is the Undergraduate program webpage: https://www.lasalle.edu/catalog/undergraduate/school-of-arts-and-sciences/department-of-psychology/psychology/#ftoc-program-description We welcome candidates from underrepresented groups and/or with expertise in and a demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and social justice initiatives. Please upload a letter of intent that describes your teaching interests and includes examples of efforts to promote a diverse and inclusive teaching and learning environment. Additionally, please upload a curriculum vitae, and evaluations of teaching if available. Please also provide contact information for three professional references. Should a review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Undergraduate Psychology, History and Systems of Psychology (in person) Department 215510 - Psychology Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0153P Position Summary La Salle University’s Psychology department has a need for an instructor for an undergraduate, in-person section of PSY 430 “History and Systems of Psychology” at the undergraduate level for Spring 2024 . The course description is as follows: This course examines the beginnings and development of psychology as a science and profession; psychology’s historical roots in philosophy, biology, and national culture. La Salle University is a Lasallian Catholic university committed to the principle that all knowledge is practical and empowering, filled with the capacity to transform lives. Anchored in the living tradition of the Brothers of the Christian Schools and in association with a diverse and inclusive learning community, our mission is to educate the whole person by fostering a rigorous free search for truth. La Salle, in affirming the value of both liberal arts and professional studies, prepares students for the lifelong pursuit and exploration of wisdom, knowledge, and faith that lead to engaged and fulfilling lives marked by a commitment to the common good. The University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect, and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. We welcome candidates whose experience in research, teaching, and service has prepared them to contribute to our department’s commitment to building a culturally diverse intellectual community. For more information about the Psychology department, please visit https://www.lasalle.edu/psychology . Essential Duties Teach assigned course(s). Prepare course materials consistent with departmental learning objectives. Provide timely grading and feedback to students. Provide guidance and support to students. Required Qualifications Required of instructors in ALL programs: Knowledge and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Multicultural competence and training. Undergraduate Program: Master’s degree (M.A.) or above in psychology or in a closely related field. Ability to teach in-person on La Salle’s main campus Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in psychology or a closely related field. Previous experience teaching at the collegiate level. Specialized knowledge of Biopsychology Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours Special Instructions to Applicant This is a course specific position announcement for an in-person section of PSY 430 “History and Systems of Psychology” at the undergraduate level for Spring 2024 . The course description is as follows: This course examines the beginnings and development of psychology as a science and profession; psychology’s historical roots in philosophy, biology, and national culture. If you are interested in other teaching opportunities in Psychology, please see the general Psychology Undergraduate position announcement. There are other ads for specific pools for teaching in the Masters and Doctoral programs. Here is the Undergraduate program webpage: https://www.lasalle.edu/catalog/undergraduate/school-of-arts-and-sciences/department-of-psychology/psychology/#ftoc-program-description We welcome candidates from underrepresented groups and/or with expertise in and a demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and social justice initiatives. Please upload a letter of intent that describes your teaching interests and includes examples of efforts to promote a diverse and inclusive teaching and learning environment. Additionally, please upload a curriculum vitae, and evaluations of teaching if available. Please also provide contact information for three professional references. Should a review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 11/02/2023 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Teaching Evaluations Transcript(s) Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest degree that you hold? High School Diploma BA or BS degree (college degree) Master's degree in Psychology or a related field Doctorate in a field related to psychology or counseling Doctorate in Psychology Doctorate in Counselor Education, Mental Health Counseling, or related (CACREP accredited) Doctorate in Marriage and Family, Couples Therapy, or related (COAMFT accredited) Other * If your answer to the above questions was \"other,\" please explain. (Open Ended Question) * What courses have you taught before and at what level? Please list them. (Open Ended Question) * What are your qualifications for teaching an undergraduate course on the history and systems of psychology? (Open Ended Question) * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/6375": {
      "title": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Coordinator of Visit Experience",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Coordinator of Visit Experience Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Coordinator of Visit Experience Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. La Salle University offers its eligible employees comprehensive medical and dental plans, employer paid life and disability insurance, retirement benefits, generous paid time off (vacation, sick leave, and holidays), and tuition benefits such as no cost undergraduate and graduate degree programs for its employees (with no wait period) and no cost undergraduate degree programs for its employees’ dependents (after completing the required years of service). Position Details Position Overview Position Title Coordinator of Visit Experience Department 522000 - Admissions Position Type Regular Position Classification Full-Time, 12 months Grant/Gift Funded (all or a portion)? No If Temporary or Grant Funded, Start Date and End Date Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number S1456P Position Summary The Coordinator of Visit Experience serves as the operational lead for campus visit programs, admissions events, and student visitor experience initiatives. Providing direct support to the Director of Visit Experience, this position oversees the daily execution of visit operations, develops student leaders, coordinates large-scale events, and partners with departments across the university to create welcoming, organized, inclusive and engaging experiences for prospective students and their families. The role also entails building trainings for all students on the topics of professionalism, public speaking skills, and polished behaviors for the workforce and visitor facing environment. The Coordinator of Visit Experience must have the ability to interact in a positive and professional manner with students, faculty, administrators, staff and the public. It is critical that the coordinator possesses and utilizes excellent customer service as it relates to hosting campus guests, the ability to support and plan large-scale events, and has an eye for detail. Essential Duties Essential Duties: Visitor Experience Operations Coordinate and support the prospective student visit experience, including daily campus tours, group visits, special events, and other recruitment activities. Plan and execute school and community group visits from start to finish, including scheduling, reserving campus spaces, coordinating student tour guides, and communications. Ensure daily visitor logistics are in place, including reserved parking signage, parking passes, visitor communications, and other hospitality-related details. Manage inventory of visit and event materials. Regularly assess admissions events and visit programs, recommending improvements based on feedback, observations, and previous successes. Offer creative ideas and process improvements that enhance visitor engagement, event quality, and operational effectiveness. Event Planning & Logistics Assist in the planning and execution of all major admissions events and campus visit programs. Ensure event information across websites, emails, and other communication platforms is accurate and up to date. Assist with the planning and execution of university-wide events as requested, including leading assigned event components and coordinating staff and student assignments. Student Leadership & Development Provide daily supervision and support for the Admissions Campus Explorers ( ACE ) and Student Team for Admissions and Recruitment ( STAR ) student staff. Design, facilitate, and continuously improve training and professional development for ACE and STAR student employees, with an emphasis on professionalism, public speaking, customer service, and visitor engagement. Develop and maintain weekly student work schedules, assign daily responsibilities, monitor progress, and provide coaching and performance feedback. Foster student leadership by mentoring and developing student employees to serve as effective representatives for La Salle University. Cross-Campus Partnerships & Communication Build and maintain collaborative relationships with Enrollment staff and university partners (staff, faculty, vendors, etc.) to ensure admissions events and visit programs are effectively planned and executed. Provide day-to-day operational support to the Visit Experience team, collaborating with professional and student staff to ensure successful execution of department initiatives. Collaborate with various departments to enhance the prospective student experience and support campus recruitment initiatives. Secondary Responsibilities Work collaboratively with other divisional and University-wide departments to enhance the student experience, especially related to on campus recruitment activities. Maintain the Enrollment Division calendar of events and communicate scheduling updates as appropriate. Ensure print and digital visit materials remain current, accurate, and aligned with university messaging. Oversee other administrative tasks. Perform other related duties as assigned. # of Direct Reports 0 Required Qualifications Associate’s degree. Ability to work as part of a team. Ability to multi-task. Mentorship skills for college-age students. Strong organizational skills with a focus on details. Excellent interpersonal skills. Experience in event planning. Experience working in higher education or a related field. Knowledge of and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Knowledge of marketing best practices in higher education related to enrollment, advancement, and institutional branding. Previous experience working in a higher education environment. Strong customer service orientation and experience in developing recruiting and communication strategies. Previous experience developing trainings for young people, working in guest relations or providing tours. Previous experience using Technolutions Slate CRM . Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours This is an on-site position that requires regular on-campus, in-person work to support departmental operations, collaborate with campus partners, and effectively perform the essential functions of the position. Evening and weekend events as needed during peak recruitment times. Will require event set ups which could include assisting with the moving of tables, chairs, etc. Special Instructions to Applicant La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. La Salle University offers its eligible employees comprehensive medical and dental plans, employer paid life and disability insurance, retirement benefits, generous paid time off (vacation, sick leave, and holidays), and tuition benefits such as no cost undergraduate and graduate degree programs for its employees (with no wait period) and no cost undergraduate degree programs for its employees’ dependents (after completing the required years of service). Posting Information Application Open Date 07/30/2026 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of customer service experience do you have? Less than 4 years 4-7 years 8-10 years 10+ years * Do you have previous experience working in higher education? Yes No * How many years of experience do you have in a related position? None Less than 3 years 3-5 years 6-8 years More than 8 years * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/5514": {
      "title": "La Salle University Job Applicant Site",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Sport Management Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Sport Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Sport Management Department 221410 - Management & Leadership Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0173P Position Summary La Salle University’s Management & Leadership discipline invites applications from qualified individuals in the sport management industry who would like to be considered for adjunct teaching opportunities. Our department is staffing undergraduate courses in areas including (but not limited to): introduction to sport management, facility and event management, esports, sports marketing, sports analytics, and sports finance. Courses are offered in-person during the day and in the evening. Interested parties should submit a cover letter, CV or résumé, and, if available, PDFs of course evaluations for courses recently taught. Essential Duties Prepare course materials consistent with departmental learning objectives. Teach assigned course(s). Provide timely grading and feedback to students. Provide guidance and support to students. Required Qualifications A master’s degree or higher in a relevant field. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience teaching at the collegiate level. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours Special Instructions to Applicant This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 12/17/2024 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Statement of Teaching Philosophy Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Briefly list your area(s) of research or teaching expertise. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have previous teaching experience in higher education? Yes No * Please indicate your availability for day or evening course offerings. Only day Only evening Flexible, with notice Only weekend seminar format * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/4688": {
      "title": "La Salle University Job Applicant Site",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Spanish Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Spanish Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Spanish Department 211810 - Global Languages,Literature&Perspec and Art Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0048P Position Summary The Department of Global Languages, Literatures, and Perspectives on our main campus is seeking part-time adjunct instructors to teach Spanish courses.  In addition to courses directed towards students learning Spanish as a second language during the day, we are also recruiting instructors to teach ( SPN 203, 204, and/or 480) for our heritage speakers in BUSCA , our associate degree program at night. Essential Duties •\tPrepare meaningful lectures and class activities for the full duration of the published class time for each class period according to academic calendar. •\tCreate a syllabus that meets the Provost’s Syllabus Checklist requirements. •\tCreate assessment activities that support the stated learning outcomes for the course. •\tAddress student questions in a timely and helpful manner. •\tUse Canvas and other technology to enhance student learning. •\tSupport and follow University policies and procedures as well as those for the department. •\tAttend faculty meetings. •\tSubmit grades and materials for assessment projects on or before stated deadlines. •\tCommunicate student concerns with personnel in the department. Required Qualifications •\tMaster’s degree in Spanish, Bilingual/Bicultural Studies, Education, or related field. Preferred Qualifications •\tPhD in Spanish, Bilingual/Bicultural Studies, Education, or related field. •\tExperience or training in teaching Spanish.  Preference will be given to candidates with experience working with heritage speakers for our courses offered to heritage speakers. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours •\tIf hired for BUSCA , instructors must be available to teach from approximately 6:00-9:15 PM as it is a program for evening students. Special Instructions to Applicant This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 10/27/2022 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education you have completed (at the time of application)? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree Doctorate Degree (e.g., PhD, PsyD, JD) None of the above Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
