    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/6397": {
      "title": "La Salle University Job Applicant Site",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Graduate Assistantships for the 2026-2027 Academic Year Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Graduate Assistantships for the 2026-2027 Academic Year Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. The links to all available Graduate Assistantship positions for the 2026-2027 academic year are included on this page. La Salle University is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, equitable, and supportive working and learning environment. We encourage individuals to apply who bring diverse perspectives and experiences, and who are dedicated to helping create an inclusive community for all. Specific duties, requirements, and details about the tuition benefit are available in each posting. Please review all information carefully. Position Details Position Overview Position Title Graduate Assistantships for the 2026-2027 Academic Year Department 311200 - Office of Human Resources Position Type Temporary Position Classification Temporary Grant/Gift Funded (all or a portion)? No If Temporary or Grant Funded, Start Date and End Date Assigned semester(s) - see individual postings Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number S1439P Position Summary Graduate Assistants are enrolled students in a La Salle Master’s program, in good standing with the University, who are student employees doing work that is related to their course of study in exchange for compensation and a tuition benefit. The Chief Extern position is the only graduate assistantship available to doctoral students. For Regular GA positions: Regular GAs are generally expected to work 20 hours per week Tuition benefits are 2 courses if working in the fall and 2 courses if working in the spring. For Half-Time GA positions: Half-Time GAs are generally expected to work 10 hours per week. Tuition benefits are 1 course if working in the fall and 1 course if working in the spring. Please note certain positions may be required to live in and are provided University housing based on their job responsibilities and some positions may have the option to live in for taking on additional responsibilities. Specific information is listed within each posting. All La Salle Graduate Assistants are permitted to work no more than 20 hours per week and may not hold any other on-campus job. Acceptance of the tuition benefit provided will replace any other scholarship awards or discounts. To review the duties and qualifications required for each assistantship, and to apply for an assistantship, please visit the individual links below. Positions available for the 2026-2027 academic year, beginning in Fall 2026 are as follows: Graduate Assistant, Academic Support for Student Athletes (Half-Time) – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Advancement Operations Graduate Assistant, Alumni Engagement – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Athletic Communications – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Athletic Digital Media – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Athletic Facilities and Operations – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Athletic Fan and Community Engagement – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Campus Engagement (Events and Marketing) – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Campus Engagement (Fraternity and Sorority Life) – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Campus Recreation (2 positions) Graduate Assistant, Career Center – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Chief Extern, PsyD Clinic (Half-Time) – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Commuter and Off-Campus Student Engagement – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Enrollment Management – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Enterprise Applications – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Field Hockey – FILLED Graduate Assistant, First Year Experience, Belonging, & Campus Life Operations – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Honors Program (Half-Time) Graduate Assistant, Housing Operations (Live-In Required) – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Human Resources – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Institutional Research & Analytics Graduate Assistant, International & Transfer Admissions – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Marketing and Communications – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Men’s Basketball - FILLED Graduate Assistant, Men’s Soccer – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Mission, Diversity & Inclusion (3 positions) Graduate Assistant, Residence Life / Graduate Hall Director (5 positions) (Live-In Required) Graduate Assistant, Speech-Language-Hearing Community Clinic - FILLED Graduate Assistant, Student Conduct & Community Standards – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Student Desk Receptionist ( SDR ) Program (Live-In Required) Graduate Assistant, Student Support and the Basket - FILLED Graduate Assistant, Student Wellness Services – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Technology Support Services – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Test Proctoring (Half-Time) (2 positions) Graduate Assistant, Triathlon Graduate Assistant, Women’s Basketball – FILLED Graduate Assistant, Women’s Lacrosse Essential Duties See individual postings Secondary Responsibilities See individual postings # of Direct Reports See individual postings Required Qualifications See individual postings Preferred Qualifications See individual postings Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours See individual postings Special Instructions to Applicant The links to all available Graduate Assistantship positions for the 2026-2027 academic year are included on this page. La Salle University is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, equitable, and supportive working and learning environment. We encourage individuals to apply who bring diverse perspectives and experiences, and who are dedicated to helping create an inclusive community for all. Specific duties, requirements, and details about the tuition benefit are available in each posting. Please review all information carefully. Posting Information Application Open Date 06/12/2026 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/5824": {
      "title": "La Salle University Job Applicant Site",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Digital Arts Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Digital Arts Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Digital Arts Department 217710 - D.A.R.T. Program (Digital Arts) Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0179P Position Summary La Salle University’s Digital Arts program has an ongoing need for highly qualified adjunct faculty to teach a variety of courses each semester on an “as needed” basis. Courses generally taught by adjunct faculty may include: web and interactive design, digital photography, digital audio, basic design, animation, color theory, typography, and other courses as needed. These courses are generally offered in person in the daytime. For more information about the Digital Arts program, please visit https://www.lasalle.edu/programs/digital-arts/. Essential Duties • Teach assigned course(s). • Prepare course materials consistent with departmental learning objectives. • Provide timely grading and feedback to students. • Provide guidance and support to students. Required Qualifications • Bachelor’s degree in Digital Arts or closely related field. • Knowledge and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Preferred Qualifications • MFA , Master’s degree in Digital Arts, or Master’s degree in closely related field. • Previous experience teaching at the collegiate level. • Willingness to be flexible in class scheduling. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours • Some classes offered may be in the evenings, on weekends, or online. Special Instructions to Applicant This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 05/28/2025 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
