    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/4678": {
      "title": "La Salle University Job Applicant Site",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Psy. D. Program in Clinical Psychology Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Psy. D. Program in Clinical Psychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors for the Psy.D. Program in Clinical Psychology will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Here is the webpage for the Psy.D. Program in Clinical Psychology: https://www.lasalle.edu/doctor-of-psychology/ There are also other pooled position ads for teaching in the undergraduate and masters programs. Please see and apply for those positions if you are interested. We welcome candidates from underrepresented groups and/or with expertise in and a demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and social justice initiatives. Please upload a letter of intent that describes your teaching interests and includes examples of efforts to promote a diverse and inclusive teaching and learning environment. Additionally, please upload a curriculum vitae, and evaluations of teaching if available. Please also provide contact information for three professional references. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Psy. D. Program in Clinical Psychology Department 281560 - Doctoral Psychology Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0115P Position Summary La Salle University’s Psy.D. Program in Clinical Psychology has an ongoing need for highly qualified adjunct faculty to teach a variety of courses each semester on an “as needed” basis. These courses are generally offered in person, in the daytime or evenings. For more information about the Psy.D. Program, please visit https://www.lasalle.edu/doctor-of-psychology/. We welcome candidates whose experience in research, teaching, and service has prepared them to contribute to our department’s commitment to building a culturally diverse intellectual community. For more information about the Psychology department, please visit www.lasalle.edu/psychology. La Salle University is a Lasallian Catholic university committed to the principle that all knowledge is practical and empowering, filled with the capacity to transform lives. Anchored in the living tradition of the Brothers of the Christian Schools and in association with a diverse and inclusive learning community, our mission is to educate the whole person by fostering a rigorous free search for truth. La Salle, in affirming the value of both liberal arts and professional studies, prepares students for the lifelong pursuit and exploration of wisdom, knowledge, and faith that lead to engaged and fulfilling lives marked by a commitment to the common good. The University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect, and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Essential Duties Teach assigned course(s). Prepare course materials consistent with departmental learning objectives. Provide timely grading and feedback to students. Provide guidance and support to students. Required Qualifications Doctoral degree in Psychology or closely related field. Multicultural competence and training. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience teaching at the collegiate level. Willingness to be flexible in class scheduling. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours Must be able to teach in-person on La Salle’s main campus in Philadelphia, PA. Some courses are held during the evening. Special Instructions to Applicant This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors for the Psy.D. Program in Clinical Psychology will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Here is the webpage for the Psy.D. Program in Clinical Psychology: https://www.lasalle.edu/doctor-of-psychology/ There are also other pooled position ads for teaching in the undergraduate and masters programs. Please see and apply for those positions if you are interested. We welcome candidates from underrepresented groups and/or with expertise in and a demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and social justice initiatives. Please upload a letter of intent that describes your teaching interests and includes examples of efforts to promote a diverse and inclusive teaching and learning environment. Additionally, please upload a curriculum vitae, and evaluations of teaching if available. Please also provide contact information for three professional references. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 10/27/2022 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Teaching Evaluations Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education you have completed (at the time of application)? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree Doctorate Degree (e.g., PhD, PsyD, JD) None of the above * Are you able to teach in-person 1-2 days per week on La Salle's Main Campus in Philadelphia, PA? Yes No * The next question will ask you to indicate which doctoral level  courses you are both qualified and willing to teach. The descriptions of these courses can be found on the following webpage. You may want to open it in a separate window before answering the next question. https://www.lasalle.edu/catalog/graduate/doctorates/doctor-of-psychology-in-clinical-psychology-psy-d/#ftoc-course-descriptions If you would also like to teach in the undergraduate and/or master's programs, please see the pooled position ads for those programs. Was this information helpful helpful to you? Yes No * Which of the following Psy.D. Program courses are you qualified and willing to teach? Course descriptions can be found at https://www.lasalle.edu/catalog/graduate/doctorates/doctor-of-psychology-in-clinical-psychology-psy-d/#ftoc-course-descriptions PSY 700 - Psychotherapy I: Individual Approaches PSY 701 - Biological Bases of Behavior PSY 702 - Foundations of Psychotherapy: Mechanisms of Change and the Therapeutic Process PSY 703 - Human Behavior IV: Social Bases PSY 704 - Psychopathology I: Adult Psychopathology PSY 705 - Psychotherapy II: Group and Systemic Approaches PSY 706 - Interviewing and Psychotherapy Laboratory PSY 707 - Psychopathology II: Child and Adolescent Psychopathology PSY 708 - Human Behavior I: Developmental Bases PSY 709 - Psychological Assessment I: Cognitive Assessment PSY 710 - Psychological Assessment III: Integrative Assessment Battery PSY 711 - Human Diversity PSY 713 - Human Behavior II: Cognitive Psychology PSY 714 - Human Behavior III: Personality and Individual Differences PSY 719 - Psychological Assessment of Children and Adolescents PSY 720 - Psychological Assessment of Children and Adolescents II PSY 724 - History and Systems of Psychology PSY 730 - Psychological Assessment II: Personality and Behavioral Assessment/Objective Methods PSY 740 - Advanced Cognitive Behavior Therapy: Theory and Application PSY 741 - Advanced Seminar in Psychotherapy and Clinical Practice PSY 742 - Clinical Psychology in Primary Care PSY 743 - Clinical Hypnosis PSY 747 - Biofeedback Training and Self-Regulation PSY 750 - Psychopharmacology PSY 751 - Clinical Health Psychology I: Introduction to Behavioral Health PSY 752 - Clinical Health Psychology II: Working with Medically Ill Populations PSY 753 - Pediatric Psychology PSY 757 - Neuropsychology I: Fundamentals of Neuropsychological Assessment PSY 758 - Neuropsychology II: Administration and Interpretation of Comprehensive Batteries PSY 762 - Advanced Seminar in Clinical Child and Family Psychology PSY 765 - Child and Adolescent Psychotherapy PSY 766 - Working with Families in Clinical Psychology PSY 770 - Psychological Measurement and Statistical Analysis PSY 771 - Research Methodology PSY 782, 783 - Doctoral Practicum I/ Practicum Seminar I PSY 784 - Consultation and Education PSY 785 - Introduction to Professional Practice, Ethics and Conduct PSY 786 - Individual Human Diversity PSY 787 - Supervision and Management PSY 788, 789 - Doctoral Practicum II/Practicum Seminar II PSY 792 - Professional Ethics PSY 794, 795 - Doctoral Practicum III/Practicum Seminar III (Optional) PSY 860 - Dissertation Project Advancement PSY 861 - Diagnostic Interviewing PSY 862 - Treatment Planning and Implementation PSY 882 - Clinical Dissertation Seminar I PSY 883 - Clinical Dissertation Seminar II PSY 884 - Clinical Dissertation Seminar III * What courses have you taught before at the graduate school level? Please list them. (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/6331": {
      "title": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Assistant Professor, Nursing (Tenure Track) (5 of 5)",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Assistant Professor, Nursing (Tenure Track) (5 of 5) Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Assistant Professor, Nursing (Tenure Track) (5 of 5) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. As part of the application you will be required to submit a cover letter and curriculum vitae, and contact information for three references. La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. La Salle University offers its eligible employees comprehensive medical and dental plans, employer paid life and disability insurance, retirement benefits, generous paid time off (vacation, sick leave, and holidays), and tuition benefits such as no cost undergraduate and graduate degree programs for its employees (with no wait period) and no cost undergraduate degree programs for its employees’ dependents (after completing the required years of service). Position Details Position Overview Position Title Assistant Professor, Nursing (Tenure Track) (5 of 5) Department 231100 - Nursing Undergraduate Appointment Term Tenure Track Position Classification Full-Time, 9 months (Faculty) Grant/Gift Funded (all or a portion)? No If Temporary or Grant Funded, Start Date and End Date Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number FA202PST Position Summary The Nursing Program within the School of Nursing and Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position (9-month appointment) with teaching responsibilities across undergraduate and graduate nursing programs. Candidates with diverse areas of expertise are encouraged to apply, with particular interest in those specializing in pathophysiology, pharmacology, health assessment, psychiatric/mental health, obstetrics, and pediatrics. Essential Duties Teach assigned courses and prepare course materials consistent with departmental learning objectives. Participate in program, school, and University committees for service in line with program expectations. Establish an active research agenda in line with program expectations. Provide academic advising for students, including mentorship, guidance, and support. Attend department, school, and University meetings and functions including student recruitment events, commencement ceremonies and related activities, and other related initiatives. Secondary Responsibilities Familiarity with varied instructional delivery methods. Familiarity with the AACN Essentials (2021) and competency-based education. Required Qualifications Doctoral degree in nursing or an appropriate discipline from an accredited institution. Current registered nurse license in Pennsylvania or multistate. A minimum of five years recent classroom and clinical experience. Evidence of scholarship, other than the doctoral dissertation, may be demonstrated by contributions to the professional literature, presentations at national, state, or local meetings and/or grantsmanship. Demonstrated record of professional and clinical experience, teaching, and curriculum development. Excellent verbal and written communication, interpersonal, and leadership skills. Participation in School and/or University Committees. Participation in professional organizations at local, state, or national levels. Preferred Qualifications Familiarity with varied instructional delivery methods. Familiarity with the AACN Essentials (2021) and competency-based education. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours Evening and weekend work may be required at times, including for student recruitment events, commencement ceremonies and related activities, and other departmental initiatives. Special Instructions to Applicant As part of the application you will be required to submit a cover letter and curriculum vitae, and contact information for three references. La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. La Salle University offers its eligible employees comprehensive medical and dental plans, employer paid life and disability insurance, retirement benefits, generous paid time off (vacation, sick leave, and holidays), and tuition benefits such as no cost undergraduate and graduate degree programs for its employees (with no wait period) and no cost undergraduate degree programs for its employees’ dependents (after completing the required years of service). Posting Information Application Open Date 06/23/2026 Application Close Date 12/31/2026 Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Teaching Evaluations Transcript(s) Writing Sample/Publications (PDF) Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
