    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/6353": {
      "title": "La Salle University Job Applicant Site",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Anatomy and Physiology Lab Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Anatomy and Physiology Lab Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In your application, please include contact information for three professional (not personal) references, including a past supervisor. La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Anatomy and Physiology Lab Department 215110 - Biology and Integrated Science, Bus & Tech Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0193P Position Summary La Salle University’s Natural Sciences Department has a need for highly qualified adjunct faculty to teach one or more laboratory sections of our freshmen-level BIO 161: Anatomy and Physiology I classes in the Fall 2026 semester. These courses are primarily taken by first-year Nursing and health sciences majors. These lab sections are scheduled at the following times: Monday, 8:15 AM – 10:05 AM Monday 10:25 AM – 12:15 AM Thursday 2:00 PM – 3:50 PM Thursday 4:00 PM – 5:50 PM Classes start on 8/31/26 and run through 12/11/26. For more information about the Biology program and the Natural Sciences Department, please visit https://www.lasalle.edu/programs/biology/ Essential Duties Teach assigned laboratory section(s). Provide guidance and support to students in Anatomy and Physiology experiments. Maintain safety in the laboratory and ensure a safety-focused environment in the lab. Provide timely grading and feedback to students. Collaborate with other Anatomy and Physiology laboratory instructors in carrying out laboratory exams. Required Qualifications Master’s or PhD degree in a biology, anatomy, physiology or related field, OR Master’s or terminal degree in related degree in a field related to anatomy/physiology (MD, DO, DPt, etc) will also be considered. Knowledge and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Preferred Qualifications Experience or desire for teaching biology and/or anatomy and physiology courses, particularly at the college-level. Experience working or teaching in a scientific laboratory. Knowledge or experience teaching anatomy and physiology laboratory courses. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours The job requires the ability to teach lab sections of A&P. The job requires movement around the classroom or laboratory, and possibly lifting heavy objects such as anatomy models or microscopes. It may be necessary for the position to teach an evening class of A&P. Special Instructions to Applicant In your application, please include contact information for three professional (not personal) references, including a past supervisor. La Salle University is dedicated to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment where all individuals can thrive. We seek candidates who will contribute to a positive, inclusive, and supportive community, and who are committed to working collaboratively with students, fostering critical thinking, supporting their success, and helping them realize their full potential. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 07/19/2026 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Portfolio (PDF) Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? blackperspective.com disabilitysolutionstalent.org disabledperson.com employdiversity.com hercjobs.org higheredjobs.com hireourheros.com hispanic-today.com indeed.com jofdav.com (Job Opportunities for Disabled Veterans) La Salle Website monster.com Referred by a Current or Former Employee Referred by a Friend or Family Member usmilitarypipeline.com veteransenterprise.com vetjobs.com wib-i.com (Women in Business & Industry) womenforhire.com Other - Academic or Professional Publication Other - Agency or Search Firm Referral Other - Diversity Association/Publication Website Other - Conference or Career Fair Other - Local Newspaper Other - Internet Site Not Listed Above Other - Professional Affiliation/Trade Website * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this questions does not apply, please enter \"N/A\". (Open Ended Question) Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
