    "https://lasalle.peopleadmin.com/postings/4641": {
      "title": "La Salle University Job Applicant Site",
      "description": "La Salle University Applicant Site | Adjunct Faculty, Education Skip to Main Content La Salle University Job Applicant Site Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Announcements Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs La Salle Website La Salle Human Resources Annual Security Report Adjunct Faculty, Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . Position Details Position Overview Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Education Department 211610 - Education Position Description/Posting Details Posting Number A0045P Position Summary The Education Department seeks adjuncts in the areas of Early Childhood, Middle Level, and Secondary Education for both undergraduate and graduate courses. Candidates with expertise in special education/disability studies, literacy/ ELA , math, and social justice in education are of special interest. We are also seeking certified educators to supervise student teachers in elementary, middle, and high schools. Essential Duties Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Education. Adjuncts can teach up to 9 credits of coursework or equivalent responsibilities. Courses are offered both day and evening. Supervisor responsibilities include no fewer than 4 observations, not including beginning, midterm, and final meetings with the student teacher and cooperating teacher. Travel to schools is required. Required Qualifications • Masters degree in the area of specialization. • Three years K-12 teaching or relevant experience. Some positions may require a valid teaching certification. • Ability to participate in professional learning communities facilitated by the Director of Placements and Partnerships and Chair of Education at La Salle. We will make every attempt to accommodate scheduling conflicts when necessary. • Knowledge and commitment to the mission of La Salle University. Candidates’ qualifications will be evaluated based on the specific needs of the course or supervisory experience. Clearances and appropriate background checks will be required. Preferred Qualifications • Ph.D. in the area of specialization. • Experience teaching coursework in higher education contexts. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours Travel to La Salle and to schools using personal transportation. Special Instructions to Applicant This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 10/27/2022 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education you have completed (at the time of application)? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree Doctorate Degree (e.g., PhD, PsyD, JD) None of the above Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 19141 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
