nd, if available, PDFs of course evaluations for courses recently taught. Essential Duties •\tTeach assigned course(s). •\tPrepare course materials consistent with departmental learning objectives. •\tProvide timely grading and feedback to students. •\tProvide guidance and support to students. Required Qualifications •\tMaster’s degree or higher in a relevant field. Preferred Qualifications •\tPrevious experience teaching at the collegiate level. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours Special Instructions to Applicant This is a pooled position from which Adjunct Instructors will be selected when/if a need arises in the department. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted directly. These pools are closed down annually during the summer and you will receive notification that a refreshed application is needed for you to continue to be considered. La Salle University embraces diversity and seeks candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports a fully inclusive, equitable, and diverse working and learning environment. We strongly encourage individuals from underrepresented and/or marginalized identities to apply . HR/Comp Compensation Information Position Classification Part-Time, Semesterly Basis FLSA Classification Exempt Pay Basis Salary Position Group Faculty Posting Information Application Open Date 10/10/2022 Application Close Date Application Open To Internal and External Applicants Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Portfolio (PDF) Teaching Evaluations Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education you have completed (at the time of application)? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree Doctorate Degree (e.g., PhD, PsyD, JD) None of the above Return to Top 1900 W. Olney Avenue, Philadelphia, PA 